{
  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "The current best (config_031: scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted; acc=0.678) shows that weighted fusion and multiprofile aggregation are strong contributors. However, the image encoder (ResNet50) performed very poorly in isolation (config_010: acc=0.208), raising the question of whether the image modality's contribution in the multimodal setting is bottlenecked by encoder capacity. Config_037 is a clean, single-variable extension of config_031 that swaps ResNet50 for the much stronger Imagenet ViT-L while keeping all other settings identical (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted). This directly tests whether upgrading the image encoder unlocks additional signal that ResNet50 cannot capture. If performance improves meaningfully, the image encoder becomes a key lever for further gains; if not, we can confidently rule out image-encoder quality as a bottleneck and redirect budget toward RNA encoder (scgpt) or fusion/aggregation refinements. Under a limited budget, this experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about one of the two modalities' contribution while staying anchored to the current best configuration."
}

